      "knowledge_id": "unirank-method-infnet",
      "decision": "considered",
      "rationale": "Pinned benchmark forward123-159 inspected: task hubs use multi_masks at136-139. This supports preserving task masks as a separate feedback path and limiting the estimand. No hub mechanism is adopted; original INFNet paper is link-only.",
      "transformed_mechanism": "None; masks and incumbent routing stay unchanged. The new input-level treatment isolates explicit action-code access conditional on those masks.",
      "variant_names": [],
      "nearest_work_difference": "No layer-wise hubs or broadcast/gate changes. This is a controlled information ablation of the imported model, not a new INFNet variant or a full reproduction.",
      "falsifier": "Blind performance matching full would leave mask-mediated feedback a plausible explanation and would not refute INFNet or total feedback utility.",
